**What is it?**
High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules; both should depend on abstractions. Abstractions should not depend on details; details should depend on abstractions.

**Why does it matter?**
Direct instantiation (`new MySqlDatabase()`) tightly couples business services to specific third-party technologies, making testing and database migration painful.

**Tiny C++ Example:**
```cpp
// High-level abstraction
class IMessageSender {
public:
    virtual void send(const std::string& msg) = 0;
};

// High-level service depends on abstraction, NOT concrete SMS/Email service
class NotificationService {
    IMessageSender* sender;
public:
    NotificationService(IMessageSender* s) : sender(s) {} // Injected via constructor
    void notifyUser(const std::string& msg) { sender->send(msg); }
};
```

