### Concept Notes: Resource Sharing via Flyweights & Centralized Mediation
**What is it?**
Flyweight shares common immutable state among thousands of objects to drastically cut memory usage. Mediator centralizes complex communication between many peer objects into a single coordination point.

**Why does it matter?**
Prevents out-of-memory errors in high-volume systems and untangles dense "many-to-many" web relationships into clean "many-to-one" connections.

**Tiny C++ Example:**
```cpp
